        'slug' => 'deployment-playbook',
        'title' => 'The TECHBISS deployment playbook',
        'type' => 'Guide', 'topic' => 'Operations', 'accent' => 'teal',
        'author' => 'Rashid Al-Amin', 'author_role' => 'Chief Delivery Officer',
        'read_minutes' => 10, 'featured' => 1, 'published_at' => '2026-08-05',
        'excerpt' => 'The checklist every TECHBISS platform passes before it takes production traffic — including the pre-flight the Advanced Installer runs for you.',
        'body' => "<p>Every platform we deploy, whether a bespoke engagement or a Marketplace product installed by a customer, passes the same pre-flight. This is that checklist, with the reasoning behind each item.</p><h2>Before you install</h2><ul><li><strong>Confirm the runtime.</strong> PHP 8.1 or newer, with PDO, mbstring, JSON and OpenSSL. The installer verifies these and refuses to continue if a hard requirement is missing.</li><li><strong>Confirm writable paths.</strong> The storage directory and its subdirectories must be writable by the web server user. This is the single most common installation failure.</li><li><strong>Decide your canonical URL.</strong> The installer detects it, including sub-directory installs and HTTPS behind a proxy, but you should confirm it matches what your DNS and certificate say.</li></ul><h2>During installation</h2><ul><li><strong>Let the existing-site scan run.</strong> If there is a previous installation, a WordPress site or another platform in the target directory, the installer detects it and offers migration rather than overwriting it.</li><li><strong>Test the database connection before continuing.</strong> The installer does this live; a green result means credentials, host, port and privileges are all correct.</li><li><strong>Set a real admin password.</strong> The installer enforces a minimum, but the account you create here owns the platform.</li></ul><h2>After installation</h2><ul><li><strong>Remove or lock the installer.</strong> The platform does this automatically by writing a lock file. Confirm it exists.</li><li><strong>Force HTTPS.</strong> Configuration snippets for Apache and nginx ship with the platform.</li><li><strong>Set the cache headers.</strong> Fingerprinted assets should be served immutable with a one-year max-age; HTML should be revalidated.</li><li><strong>Verify the health endpoint.</strong> <code>/health</code> returns the platform version, database connectivity and cache state. Point your monitoring at it.</li></ul><h2>Day two</h2><p>Confirm your backups actually restore. A backup you have never restored is a hypothesis, not a backup.</p>",
